Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.80,0:00:22.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎收看《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:00:20.80,0:00:22.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Today on how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.72,0:00:28.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料袋：大批量生产
Dialogue: 1,0:00:24.72,0:00:28.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Plastic bags, mass, mass, mass production.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.32,0:00:33.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,太阳能电池板：自给自足者的内行门道
Dialogue: 1,0:00:30.32,0:00:33.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Solar panels, inside knowledge for the self sufficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.16,0:00:40.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料汽油桶：长途出行的必需品
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.16,0:00:40.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Plastic petrol containers, essential when you're taking long journeys.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.38,0:00:45.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有曲棍球棍：来自工厂的劲射
Dialogue: 1,0:00:41.38,0:00:45.20,Original,,0,0,0,,And ice hockey sticks, slapshots from the factory floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.48,0:00:47.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过首先
Dialogue: 1,0:00:46.48,0:00:47.04,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.60,0:00:52.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们已成为世界各地环卫工的祸害
Dialogue: 1,0:00:49.60,0:00:52.80,Original,,0,0,0,,they've become the scourge of rubbish collectors the world over.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.76,0:00:57.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,你家里某个角落大概也堆着一堆，越积越多
Dialogue: 1,0:00:53.76,0:00:57.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Chances are there's a growing pile of them somewhere in your house.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.24,0:01:00.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,好在至少现在有了回收
Dialogue: 1,0:00:58.24,0:01:00.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Thankfully at least now there's recycling
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.32,0:01:03.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,既能减轻内疚，也能清空厨房抽屉
Dialogue: 1,0:01:00.32,0:01:03.52,Original,,0,0,0,,which can purge both the conscience and the kitchen drawer.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.40,0:01:06.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是不起眼的塑料袋
Dialogue: 1,0:01:04.40,0:01:06.08,Original,,0,0,0,,It's the humble plastic bag.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.40,0:01:13.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料袋的制作很简单
Dialogue: 1,0:01:10.40,0:01:13.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Plastic bags are made simply from granules of linear
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.76,0:01:16.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,原料是熔化的线性聚乙烯树脂颗粒
Dialogue: 1,0:01:13.76,0:01:16.08,Original,,0,0,0,,polyethylene resin that will be melted.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.84,0:01:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,他们将颗粒与其他低密度树脂混合
Dialogue: 1,0:01:17.84,0:01:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,They combine the granules with other low density
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.16,0:01:24.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,在搅拌机中拌成均匀的材料
Dialogue: 1,0:01:20.16,0:01:24.96,Original,,0,0,0,,resins in this mixer, where the combination is blended into a homogenous material.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.92,0:01:39.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,颗粒在挤出机中熔化，被加热到 240 摄氏度
Dialogue: 1,0:01:33.92,0:01:39.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Granules melt in the extruder, which heats them to a temperature of 240 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.76,0:01:50.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,聚乙烯薄膜呈管状向上鼓出，长达数百米
Dialogue: 1,0:01:45.76,0:01:50.48,Original,,0,0,0,,A polythene film billows upwards in the form of a tube, several hundred metres long.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.16,0:01:59.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料逐渐冷却下来
Dialogue: 1,0:01:58.16,0:01:59.76,Original,,0,0,0,,When the plastic gradually cools down.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.40,0:02:01.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,辊筒将管膜压平
Dialogue: 1,0:02:00.40,0:02:01.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Rollers flatten out the tube.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:11.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,管膜被裁成两卷
Dialogue: 1,0:02:10.00,0:02:11.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The tube is cut into 2 separate rolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.76,0:02:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,聚乙烯薄膜现在易于加工
Dialogue: 1,0:02:17.76,0:02:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The polythene film is now easy to work with.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.58,0:02:25.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后刀片将薄膜切成所需宽度
Dialogue: 1,0:02:22.58,0:02:25.28,Original,,0,0,0,,A knife then cuts the film to the required width.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.34,0:02:36.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,多余的边条被回收进这根管子
Dialogue: 1,0:02:34.34,0:02:36.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The excess strip is salvaged in this tube.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.00,0:02:43.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,数百米长的薄膜就此生产并收卷
Dialogue: 1,0:02:40.00,0:02:43.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Several hundred metres of film are produced and rolled up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.32,0:02:54.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,卷满后，薄膜被裁断
Dialogue: 1,0:02:52.32,0:02:54.48,Original,,0,0,0,,When the roll is full, the film is cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.98,0:03:09.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,一整卷重 158 公斤，可制成 35000 个袋子
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.98,0:03:09.28,Original,,0,0,0,,A full roll weighs 158 kilos and can produce 35,000 bags.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.64,0:03:14.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,下一步是给袋子印刷
Dialogue: 1,0:03:12.64,0:03:14.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The next step is the printing of the bags.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.56,0:03:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种醇基油墨持续循环，以保持其粘度
Dialogue: 1,0:03:16.56,0:03:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This alcohol-based ink circulates continuously to retain.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.16,0:03:23.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,印迹由着墨辊压制而成
Dialogue: 1,0:03:20.16,0:03:23.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Its viscosity impressions are made by inking rollers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.92,0:03:27.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,每种颜色都有独立的车间
Dialogue: 1,0:03:25.92,0:03:27.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Each colour has a separate room.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.84,0:03:33.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,印刷结束后，塑料薄膜再次收卷
Dialogue: 1,0:03:29.84,0:03:33.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Once printing is over, the plastic film is rolled up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.92,0:03:37.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,卷已满，可以开始裁袋了
Dialogue: 1,0:03:33.92,0:03:37.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The roll is now full, and the cutting of bags can get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.00,0:03:42.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器每分钟生产 150 个
Dialogue: 1,0:03:40.00,0:03:42.40,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine makes 150 per minute,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.72,0:03:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,封口机用热力将袋子边缘粘合
Dialogue: 1,0:03:42.72,0:03:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,as a sealer bonds the edges of the bags together with heat.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.16,0:03:51.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,转轮拾起袋子，放到两根轴上，每根可装 250 个
Dialogue: 1,0:03:46.16,0:03:51.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The wheel picks up the bags and puts them on 2 spindles that can hold 250 each.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.44,0:03:54.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些袋子正在安装密封拉链
Dialogue: 1,0:03:51.44,0:03:54.88,Original,,0,0,0,,These bags are being fitted with a hermetic zipper.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.84,0:03:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,拉链由一块塑料垫制成，可插入槽中
Dialogue: 1,0:03:55.84,0:03:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The zipper is made from a plastic pad which inserts into a slot.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.04,0:04:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,拉链预先制好，逐步展开
Dialogue: 1,0:04:03.04,0:04:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Made in advance, the zipper is unrolled progressively.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.80,0:04:14.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,拉链带被裁断，在 180 摄氏度下热封到袋子上
Dialogue: 1,0:04:08.80,0:04:14.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The zipper strip is cut and heat bonded to the bag at 180 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.84,0:04:18.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,快速检查一切是否正常运转
Dialogue: 1,0:04:15.84,0:04:18.40,Original,,0,0,0,,A quick check that everything's functioning as it should.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.76,0:04:27.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,在另一车间，制作带提手的塑料袋
Dialogue: 1,0:04:23.76,0:04:27.28,Original,,0,0,0,,In another department, plastic bags with handles are created.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.24,0:04:30.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,印好的袋子在这些辊上输送
Dialogue: 1,0:04:28.24,0:04:30.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Printed bags circulate on these rollers.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.42,0:04:40.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,封边机在封住两侧的同时，也把袋子塑成所需的形状
Dialogue: 1,0:04:35.42,0:04:40.00,Original,,0,0,0,,A machine that seals the sides gives the bags the desired shape at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.04,0:04:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后另一台带冲头的机器冲出提手孔
Dialogue: 1,0:04:44.04,0:04:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Then another machine with a punch cuts the handle holes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.84,0:04:53.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,袋子在 150 摄氏度下热封并裁切
Dialogue: 1,0:04:49.84,0:04:53.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Bags are heat sealed and cut at 150 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.04,0:04:57.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里正在成型更多款式
Dialogue: 1,0:04:55.04,0:04:57.44,Original,,0,0,0,,And here, further designs are being formed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.52,0:05:03.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,袋子的一端被热封
Dialogue: 1,0:05:01.52,0:05:03.20,Original,,0,0,0,,One end of the bag is heat sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.96,0:05:08.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器打孔，装填时让空气排出袋子
Dialogue: 1,0:05:04.96,0:05:08.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine makes holes, which let air out of the bag when it's being filled.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.44,0:05:10.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这样它们能装得更多
Dialogue: 1,0:05:09.44,0:05:10.72,Original,,0,0,0,,This allows them to hold more.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.60,0:05:16.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时，冲压机冲出提手孔
Dialogue: 1,0:05:13.60,0:05:16.24,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, a stamper cuts the handle holes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.40,0:05:24.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,袋子被裁成所需尺寸
Dialogue: 1,0:05:22.40,0:05:24.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Bags are cut to the required size,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.40,0:05:26.66,Translation,,0,0,0,,同时自动封合另一端
Dialogue: 1,0:05:24.40,0:05:26.66,Original,,0,0,0,,automatically sealing the other side of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.48,0:05:34.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,就这么一家小厂，一天竟能生产出多达 100 万个袋子
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.48,0:05:34.72,Original,,0,0,0,,In just a single day, this relatively small factory can produce a staggering one million bags.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.36,0:05:47.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,不久之前，还只有环保人士和嬉皮士呼吁推广太阳能
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.36,0:05:47.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Not so long ago, it was just the greens and hippies calling for its introduction.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.56,0:05:54.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,太阳能这个概念，一度看似要么是实现所有梦想的答案，要么只是昙花一现
Dialogue: 1,0:05:48.56,0:05:54.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Solar energy was a concept that seemed to either be the answer to all our dreams, or just a flash in the pan.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.20,0:05:57.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,而答案其实介于两者之间
Dialogue: 1,0:05:55.20,0:05:57.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Well, the answer is somewhere in the middle.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.08,0:06:00.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎了解太阳能电池板
Dialogue: 1,0:05:58.08,0:06:00.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the solar panel.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.64,0:06:01.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,家家户户都该装一块
Dialogue: 1,0:06:00.64,0:06:01.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Every house should have one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.24,0:06:06.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,太阳能的原理很简单
Dialogue: 1,0:06:04.24,0:06:06.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The concept of solar energy is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.28,0:06:13.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,面板吸收太阳光线，通过安装的光伏电池将其转化为电能
Dialogue: 1,0:06:07.28,0:06:13.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Panels soak up the sun's rays and transform it into electricity with mounted photovoltaic cells.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.96,0:06:17.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,蓝色板体由晶硅制成
Dialogue: 1,0:06:14.96,0:06:17.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The blue plate is made of crystalline silicon,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.68,0:06:19.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,凹槽则是导电体
Dialogue: 1,0:06:17.68,0:06:19.04,Original,,0,0,0,,and the grooves are the conductors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.42,0:06:29.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,要制作太阳能电池板，需将若干模组连接起来
Dialogue: 1,0:06:25.42,0:06:29.60,Original,,0,0,0,,To make a solar panel, several of the modules have to be connected together,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.16,0:06:31.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,并涂上助焊剂
Dialogue: 1,0:06:30.16,0:06:31.52,Original,,0,0,0,,applied with a soldering flux.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.84,0:06:38.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,用电烙铁加热焊丝
Dialogue: 1,0:06:35.84,0:06:38.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The solder wire is heated with an iron,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.16,0:06:39.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,模组被放置在一个特制支架上
Dialogue: 1,0:06:38.16,0:06:39.84,Original,,0,0,0,,and the modules are placed on a special support.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.60,0:06:51.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,焊接完成后，模组在 60 摄氏度的水中进行超声波清洗
Dialogue: 1,0:06:45.60,0:06:51.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Once the soldering is done, the modules are cleaned by ultrasound in water at 60 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.16,0:06:55.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,干燥并彻底清洁后，即可进行下一步加工
Dialogue: 1,0:06:52.16,0:06:55.60,Original,,0,0,0,,When dried and perfectly clean, they're ready to be modified.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.52,0:07:02.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在可以着手将模组焊接在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:06:59.52,0:07:02.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they can proceed with soldering the modules together.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.52,0:07:07.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先涂上助焊剂，以提高焊接质量
Dialogue: 1,0:07:03.52,0:07:07.12,Original,,0,0,0,,First, a flux is applied, which improves the quality of the soldering.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.08,0:07:15.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,操作者手法娴熟，组装出 4 组模组，每组 9 块
Dialogue: 1,0:07:10.08,0:07:15.12,Original,,0,0,0,,With great dexterity, 4 groups are assembled, composing of 9 modules each.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.16,0:07:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这样共 36 块模组串联焊接起来
Dialogue: 1,0:07:16.16,0:07:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,In this way, 36 modules are soldered and connected in series.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.38,0:07:26.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,模组首尾相接，必须小心操作
Dialogue: 1,0:07:22.38,0:07:26.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Modules are assembled end to end and have to be handled with great care.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.40,0:07:32.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,用电压表逐一检测每段电压
Dialogue: 1,0:07:28.40,0:07:32.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Using a voltmeter, the voltage of each section is verified.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.28,0:07:37.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时若发现问题，很容易重新焊接
Dialogue: 1,0:07:33.28,0:07:37.52,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, it's easy to remake a solder connection if there's a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.48,0:07:43.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,若电压达标，吸盘会吸附到 9 排模组上
Dialogue: 1,0:07:38.48,0:07:43.52,Original,,0,0,0,,If the voltage is adequate, suction grips attach themselves to the 9 rows of modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.16,0:07:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这样就不会污染电池片表面
Dialogue: 1,0:07:44.16,0:07:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,In this way, there's no danger of contaminating the screens.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.96,0:07:53.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,模组被安放到指定位置
Dialogue: 1,0:07:51.96,0:07:53.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The modules are placed in position.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.80,0:07:56.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后插入一条金属带
Dialogue: 1,0:07:54.80,0:07:56.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Then a metallic strip is inserted,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.72,0:07:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,作为导体连接所有模组
Dialogue: 1,0:07:56.72,0:07:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,which acts as a conductor, linking all the modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.00,0:08:08.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,焊接一处即可完成连接
Dialogue: 1,0:08:06.00,0:08:08.24,Original,,0,0,0,,A soldered connection finishes the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.28,0:08:11.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,再铺上一块透明夹层玻璃
Dialogue: 1,0:08:09.28,0:08:11.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Then a transparent sheet of layered glass is set.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.76,0:08:17.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,它作为坚固透明的基板，用于支撑模组
Dialogue: 1,0:08:13.76,0:08:17.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This serves as a rigid transparent form, which will support the modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.12,0:08:30.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,基板的刚性由一层层压板进一步增强
Dialogue: 1,0:08:27.12,0:08:30.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The rigidity of the form is enhanced by a laminate sheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.80,0:08:39.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后再覆一层密封膜加以保护
Dialogue: 1,0:08:36.80,0:08:39.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, a sealing film is applied for protection.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.40,0:08:50.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了层压加固太阳能电池板
Dialogue: 1,0:08:48.40,0:08:50.40,Original,,0,0,0,,To laminate and stiffen the solar panel,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.80,0:08:55.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,将其放入密封加热炉中，抽空空气
Dialogue: 1,0:08:50.80,0:08:55.20,Original,,0,0,0,,it's placed in a hermetically sealed heated oven, with the air vacuumed out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.16,0:08:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,面板将在 80 摄氏度下烘烤 15 分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:08:56.16,0:08:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The panel will cook at 80 degrees centigrade for 15 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.56,0:09:08.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,出炉后，所有部件便粘结在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:09:04.56,0:09:08.48,Original,,0,0,0,,And once it exits the oven, all the components are bonded together.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.84,0:09:12.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,面板被放入太阳光模拟器中进行测试
Dialogue: 1,0:09:09.84,0:09:12.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The panel is placed in a solar simulator for testing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.88,0:09:19.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,太阳能电池板的正负触点连接电压表
Dialogue: 1,0:09:14.88,0:09:19.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Negative and positive contacts of the solar panel are connected to a voltmeter.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.48,0:09:28.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,面板插入模拟器
Dialogue: 1,0:09:26.48,0:09:28.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The panel is inserted into the simulator,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.04,0:09:30.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,一盏强力灯将照射它
Dialogue: 1,0:09:29.04,0:09:30.80,Original,,0,0,0,,and a powerful lamp will illuminate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.92,0:09:36.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,电压表准备就绪，以确认面板能提供所需的电流
Dialogue: 1,0:09:31.92,0:09:36.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The voltmeter is ready to make sure that the panel supplies the electric current required.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.52,0:09:41.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,不同的面板需要不同的构造
Dialogue: 1,0:09:39.52,0:09:41.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Different panels require different builds.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.88,0:09:46.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里正在制造非晶硅面板
Dialogue: 1,0:09:42.88,0:09:46.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, an amorphous silicon panel is being constructed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.28,0:10:04.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,面板放入塑料边框并粘合固定
Dialogue: 1,0:10:01.28,0:10:04.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The panel is placed into a plastic frame and glued in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.36,0:10:12.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后拧紧边框，使其不会移动
Dialogue: 1,0:10:09.36,0:10:12.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the frame is screwed tight so that it won't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.32,0:10:20.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,太阳能电池板装入塑料边框后便告完成
Dialogue: 1,0:10:16.32,0:10:20.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The solar panel is put into a plastic frame and is now completed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.24,0:10:25.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造这块面板大约需要 1 小时工时
Dialogue: 1,0:10:22.24,0:10:25.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Fabrication of this panel will have required about 1 hour of work,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.40,0:10:31.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,而随着双能源住宅逐渐成为必需品，需求量势必增长
Dialogue: 1,0:10:26.40,0:10:31.36,Original,,0,0,0,,and demand is sure to heighten as dual energy houses start to become a necessity.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.00,0:10:37.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是《造物小百科》：塑料汽油桶
Dialogue: 1,0:10:34.00,0:10:37.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up in how it's made: plastic petrol containers,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.04,0:10:43.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,回收塑料和一个简单的模具，就能让你免于大老远跑去加油站
Dialogue: 1,0:10:39.04,0:10:43.44,Original,,0,0,0,,recycled plastic and a simple mould can save you a long walk to the petrol station.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.20,0:10:49.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有曲棍球棍，以 150 公里/时的速度挥击
Dialogue: 1,0:10:45.20,0:10:49.68,Original,,0,0,0,,And ice hockey sticks, travelling at speeds of 150 kilometres an hour,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.16,0:10:52.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,要打出那样一记重击，背后凝聚着大量工程心血
Dialogue: 1,0:10:50.16,0:10:52.88,Original,,0,0,0,,a lot of engineering goes into packing that sort of punch.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.32,0:10:55.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,广告之后见
Dialogue: 1,0:10:54.32,0:10:55.12,Original,,0,0,0,,See you after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.20,0:11:06.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:05.20,0:11:06.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.32,0:11:10.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后我们来看曲棍球棍
Dialogue: 1,0:11:08.32,0:11:10.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Later we look at ice hockey sticks,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.88,0:11:15.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些优雅的弯曲木棍，挥击时速高达 150 公里
Dialogue: 1,0:11:10.88,0:11:15.84,Original,,0,0,0,,elegant pieces of curved wood wielded at speeds of 150 kilometres an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.36,0:11:17.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过首先
Dialogue: 1,0:11:17.36,0:11:17.92,Original,,0,0,0,,But first.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.08,0:11:24.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,你的油箱几乎见底，却赌着剩下的汽油
Dialogue: 1,0:11:20.08,0:11:24.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Your tank's almost empty, but you're gambling you'll have enough petrol
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.24,0:11:26.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,还能勉强撑到更远一点的地方
Dialogue: 1,0:11:24.24,0:11:26.24,Original,,0,0,0,,to make it just that little bit further.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.60,0:11:30.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,好吧，当你踏上那条通往最近加油站的漫漫长路时
Dialogue: 1,0:11:27.60,0:11:30.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Well, when you're on that long walk to the nearest petrol station,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.72,0:11:36.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,你会庆幸有人想出妙招，生产这些方便的塑料汽油桶
Dialogue: 1,0:11:30.72,0:11:36.32,Original,,0,0,0,,you'll be glad someone had the bright idea of manufacturing these handy plastic petrol containers.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.84,0:11:42.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料汽油桶由颗粒制成
Dialogue: 1,0:11:39.84,0:11:42.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Plastic petrol containers are made from granules
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.72,0:11:46.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,颗粒由浓缩色料和抗紫外线添加剂组成
Dialogue: 1,0:11:42.72,0:11:46.88,Original,,0,0,0,,composed of concentrated colourant and a UV resistant additive.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.68,0:11:49.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们与白色颗粒混合
Dialogue: 1,0:11:47.68,0:11:49.44,Original,,0,0,0,,They're mixed with white granules,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.60,0:11:52.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,白色颗粒是主要原料，称为高密度聚乙烯
Dialogue: 1,0:11:49.60,0:11:52.48,Original,,0,0,0,,which is the primary material called high density
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.56,0:11:56.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,以及磨碎的回收塑料
Dialogue: 1,0:11:52.56,0:11:56.40,Original,,0,0,0,,polyethylene, and recycled plastic which has been ground up.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.36,0:12:01.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,全部倒入这台研磨机，混合在一起熔化
Dialogue: 1,0:11:57.36,0:12:01.28,Original,,0,0,0,,It's all dumped into this milling machine, mixed together and melted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.28,0:12:07.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,熔化的塑料将被吹入这个模具
Dialogue: 1,0:12:05.28,0:12:07.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The melted plastic will be blown into this mould
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.92,0:12:11.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具由高密度优质铝制成，称为航空级铝
Dialogue: 1,0:12:07.92,0:12:11.92,Original,,0,0,0,,made of high quality dense aluminium called an aviation type.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.76,0:12:20.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,吹塑成型产生一根柔软的塑料管
Dialogue: 1,0:12:17.76,0:12:20.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The blow moulding produces a soft plastic tube.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.24,0:12:26.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料管被裁下放入模具
Dialogue: 1,0:12:24.24,0:12:26.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This is cut and placed in the mould
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.72,0:12:29.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,喷嘴将塑料注入模具内壁
Dialogue: 1,0:12:26.72,0:12:29.68,Original,,0,0,0,,where a nozzle pumps the plastic into the mould shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.28,0:12:34.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,容器脱模后沿传送带移动
Dialogue: 1,0:12:31.28,0:12:34.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The container is unmoulded and moves along on a conveyor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.36,0:12:39.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,但这不是唯一的成型方法
Dialogue: 1,0:12:37.36,0:12:39.60,Original,,0,0,0,,But that's not the only way to mould plastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.16,0:12:41.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有旋转成型法
Dialogue: 1,0:12:40.16,0:12:41.60,Original,,0,0,0,,There's the rotation method.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.44,0:12:51.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,低密度线性聚乙烯倒入模具底部
Dialogue: 1,0:12:47.44,0:12:51.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Low density linear polyethylene is poured into the bottom of the mould.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.28,0:12:57.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具盖上盖子，然后放到钢制支架上
Dialogue: 1,0:12:53.28,0:12:57.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The mould has a cover which will be closed, then placed on a steel support.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.12,0:13:04.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,支架由支臂带动，同时绕两条轴旋转
Dialogue: 1,0:12:59.12,0:13:04.08,Original,,0,0,0,,This support is articulated by an arm on 2 rotation axes simultaneously.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.28,0:13:08.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一动作让塑料粉末均匀分布在整个模具内
Dialogue: 1,0:13:05.28,0:13:08.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This action allows the plastic powder to distribute itself throughout the mould.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.40,0:13:20.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具放入 310 摄氏度的烘箱中
Dialogue: 1,0:13:15.40,0:13:20.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The mould is placed in an oven at temperatures of 310 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.28,0:13:26.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,粉末熔化约需 15 分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:13:23.28,0:13:26.08,Original,,0,0,0,,About 15 minutes is needed for the powder to melt,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.40,0:13:35.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,脱模前还需 15 分钟让工件充分冷却
Dialogue: 1,0:13:26.40,0:13:35.36,Original,,0,0,0,,and another 15 minutes to allow the piece to adequately cool before unmoulding it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.48,0:13:42.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,掀开模具盖，塑料工件脱模
Dialogue: 1,0:13:38.48,0:13:42.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The mould cover is lifted off, and the plastic piece is unmoulded.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.52,0:13:46.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里还制作其他东西
Dialogue: 1,0:13:45.52,0:13:46.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Other things are made here too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.92,0:13:50.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里制作的是健身车护罩
Dialogue: 1,0:13:47.92,0:13:50.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Here they create a cover for a stationary bicycle.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.52,0:13:55.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,用气动工具切割开口
Dialogue: 1,0:13:53.52,0:13:55.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Openings are cut with a pneumatic tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.60,0:14:02.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,钻好孔后，护罩就完成了
Dialogue: 1,0:13:59.60,0:14:02.96,Original,,0,0,0,,When the holes have been drilled, the casing is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.40,0:14:14.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们回到吹塑成型工艺
Dialogue: 1,0:14:12.40,0:14:14.72,Original,,0,0,0,,We return to the blow moulding process.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.68,0:14:32.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,会残留废料，必须清除
Dialogue: 1,0:14:29.68,0:14:32.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Residues build up, which have to be eliminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.50,0:14:36.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些多余边料用这把小锯裁掉
Dialogue: 1,0:14:33.50,0:14:36.32,Original,,0,0,0,,These surplus pieces are cut with this small saw,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.12,0:14:40.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,变硬的废料随后被送去粉碎成颗粒
Dialogue: 1,0:14:37.12,0:14:40.60,Original,,0,0,0,,and the now hardened scraps are sent to be reduced into granules,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.32,0:14:45.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些颗粒将重新加入搅拌机，用于制造其他塑料容器
Dialogue: 1,0:14:41.32,0:14:45.00,Original,,0,0,0,,which will be newly added to the mixer to make other plastic containers.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.48,0:15:02.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,一台小型气钻在容器上钻出排气孔
Dialogue: 1,0:14:59.48,0:15:02.44,Original,,0,0,0,,A small pneumatic drill pierces the container's vent hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.76,0:15:10.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,容器继续在传送带上行进，那里有一组机械臂在等候
Dialogue: 1,0:15:05.76,0:15:10.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The containers continue their journey by conveyor, where a set of robotic arms awaits.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.32,0:15:19.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,最终部件被装上，例如倾倒嘴
Dialogue: 1,0:15:16.32,0:15:19.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The final elements are attached, such as the pouring spout.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.16,0:15:31.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后一个带橡胶垫圈的瓶塞防止渗漏
Dialogue: 1,0:15:28.16,0:15:31.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Then a stopper, equipped with a rubber washer, prevents leaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.44,0:15:41.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，瓶口盖子自动拧紧到位
Dialogue: 1,0:15:37.44,0:15:41.52,Original,,0,0,0,,And finally, the cap of the neck is automatically screwed into place.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.52,0:15:49.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,视模具厚度而定
Dialogue: 1,0:15:47.52,0:15:49.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Depending on the thickness of the mould,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.92,0:15:52.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,每小时可生产 120 个容器
Dialogue: 1,0:15:49.92,0:15:52.80,Original,,0,0,0,,120 containers an hour are produced.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.04,0:15:57.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,旋转成型所需时间稍长一些
Dialogue: 1,0:15:55.04,0:15:57.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The rotation process takes a little longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.16,0:16:01.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,成品容器现在可以打包交付了
Dialogue: 1,0:15:58.16,0:16:01.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Finished containers are now ready for packing and delivery.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.96,0:16:06.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,如果你还是不够聪明、忘了买一个，至少现在知道它们是怎么做的了
Dialogue: 1,0:16:01.96,0:16:06.92,Original,,0,0,0,,And if you're still not clever enough to remember to buy one, you'll at least know how they're made.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.68,0:16:18.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,很少有东西像弯曲的抛光木料那样优雅
Dialogue: 1,0:16:14.68,0:16:18.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Few things are as elegant as curved, polished wood,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.68,0:16:25.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,尤其当它以 150 公里的时速，以一记劲射直扑守门员身后时
Dialogue: 1,0:16:18.68,0:16:25.24,Original,,0,0,0,,especially when travelling at 150 kilometres an hour and driving a slap shot right past the goalie.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.60,0:16:29.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造一根曲棍球棍需要大量工程心血
Dialogue: 1,0:16:26.60,0:16:29.96,Original,,0,0,0,,A lot of engineering goes into creating an ice hockey stick
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.36,0:16:31.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,才能打出那样的力道
Dialogue: 1,0:16:30.36,0:16:31.88,Original,,0,0,0,,that packs that sort of punch.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.60,0:16:46.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,大约 1200 年前，爱尔兰人就在玩一种草地曲棍球
Dialogue: 1,0:16:40.60,0:16:46.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The Irish, some 1,200 years ago, were playing hurling, a form of hockey on grass.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:40.60,0:16:44.60,Annotation,,0,0,0,,hurling：爱尔兰传统曲棍球
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.00,0:16:55.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,17 世纪，美洲原住民玩一种用弯棍的游戏，他们称之为巴格塔韦
Dialogue: 1,0:16:49.00,0:16:55.00,Original,,0,0,0,,In the 17th century, Amerindians used curved sticks in a game they called baggataway.
Dialogue: 2,0:16:49.00,0:16:52.00,Annotation,,0,0,0,,巴格塔韦：北美原住民球戏
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.60,0:17:03.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,我们今天所知的冰球，是 1855 年由驻金士顿的英国士兵发明的
Dialogue: 1,0:16:57.60,0:17:03.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Ice hockey, as we know it today, was developed by British soldiers in 1855 at Kingston, Ontario,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.16,0:17:06.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,作为加拿大漫长冬季里的消遣
Dialogue: 1,0:17:04.16,0:17:06.80,Original,,0,0,0,,as a pastime during Canada's long winters.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.80,0:17:21.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造曲棍球棍需要将几块木料和玻璃纤维融合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:17:16.80,0:17:21.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Making a hockey stick requires the melding of several pieces of wood and fiberglass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.32,0:17:25.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些球棍都是仿照冰球名将的球棍制作的
Dialogue: 1,0:17:22.32,0:17:25.28,Original,,0,0,0,,These sticks are all modelled on great hockey professionals.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.76,0:17:32.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,杆身由一块杨木制成，上面粘上两条薄桦木片
Dialogue: 1,0:17:27.76,0:17:32.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The shaft is made of a piece of poplar onto which they glue 2 thin strips of birch.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.84,0:17:40.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,放入一个环形传送带，配有一台压机，在胶水干燥前把木片压在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:17:33.84,0:17:40.16,Original,,0,0,0,,This is placed on a circular conveyor equipped with a press, which holds the pieces together while the glue dries.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.60,0:17:46.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后一把多锯片锯将木料切成 3 根相同的杆身坯料
Dialogue: 1,0:17:41.60,0:17:46.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Then a multi-bladed saw cuts the wood into 3 identical stick shaft pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.22,0:17:56.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,杆身被送到精密砂光机，用玻璃纤维进行加固
Dialogue: 1,0:17:51.22,0:17:56.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The shafts are moved to a precision sander, where they're reinforced with fiberglass.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.28,0:18:04.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,辊子涂上一层环氧树脂胶
Dialogue: 1,0:18:01.28,0:18:04.80,Original,,0,0,0,,A roller applies a coat of epoxy resin, a type of glue,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.44,0:18:08.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后在上面铺上碳纤维增强玻璃纤维
Dialogue: 1,0:18:05.44,0:18:08.56,Original,,0,0,0,,onto which they place carbon-reinforced fiberglass.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.52,0:18:11.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,树脂干燥硬化后
Dialogue: 1,0:18:09.52,0:18:11.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Once the resin has dried and hardened,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.36,0:18:19.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,杆身放入独立模具，在 80 摄氏度的压机中烘烤 12 分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:18:12.36,0:18:19.72,Original,,0,0,0,,the stick shaft is placed in an individual mould and cooked in this press heated at 80 degrees centigrade for 12 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.84,0:18:26.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,杆身随后进入铣床，用金刚石刀头打磨圆边
Dialogue: 1,0:18:20.84,0:18:26.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The shaft then goes to a milling machine equipped with diamond-headed knives, which round the edges.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.76,0:18:31.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,杆身表面再上一层漆，凸显木纹
Dialogue: 1,0:18:26.76,0:18:31.08,Original,,0,0,0,,A finish is applied to the shaft, which brings out the grain of the wood.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.04,0:18:37.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在他们把小块木料粘在末端，用来安装拍刃
Dialogue: 1,0:18:34.04,0:18:37.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Now they glue small blocks to the end in order to attach the blade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.68,0:18:44.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,用的是聚氨酯胶，耐水耐湿，非常适合曲棍球棍
Dialogue: 1,0:18:38.68,0:18:44.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Urethane glue is used, which resists water and humidity, perfect for hockey sticks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.36,0:18:58.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,一台纵切机切开杆身和木块，以便插入拍刃
Dialogue: 1,0:18:54.36,0:18:58.52,Original,,0,0,0,,A slitter cuts the shaft and wood blocks in order to slide in the blade,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.34,0:19:06.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器将胶水和拍刃插入杆身
Dialogue: 1,0:19:02.34,0:19:06.44,Original,,0,0,0,,and a machine inserts the glue and the blade into the stick shaft.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.52,0:19:12.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,球棍放到传送带上
Dialogue: 1,0:19:10.52,0:19:12.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The stick is placed on a conveyor,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.28,0:19:15.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,送往下一道工序，同时让胶水风干
Dialogue: 1,0:19:12.28,0:19:15.76,Original,,0,0,0,,leading it to its next step and giving the glue a chance to dry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.52,0:19:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,拍刃两侧被砂磨变薄
Dialogue: 1,0:19:17.52,0:19:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Both sides of the blade are sanded to thin them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.16,0:19:25.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些球棍是冰球职业选手所用球棍的复制品
Dialogue: 1,0:19:22.16,0:19:25.36,Original,,0,0,0,,These sticks are replicas of those used by hockey professionals.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.48,0:19:31.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台数控车床根据电脑内存中储存的数据切削拍刃
Dialogue: 1,0:19:26.48,0:19:31.84,Original,,0,0,0,,This computer-controlled digital lathe cuts the blade with data stored in the computer's memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.60,0:19:41.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,拍刃现在需要弯出弧度
Dialogue: 1,0:19:39.60,0:19:41.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The blade now has to be curved.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.16,0:19:47.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,蒸 1 分钟，让水分渗入木材，使其变软
Dialogue: 1,0:19:42.16,0:19:47.44,Original,,0,0,0,,It's steamed for a minute, allowing humidity to penetrate the wood, making it flexible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.40,0:19:50.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后拍刃放入这个弧形模具
Dialogue: 1,0:19:48.40,0:19:50.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the blade is placed in this curved mould,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.28,0:19:54.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,在 55 摄氏度下加热 50 秒
Dialogue: 1,0:19:51.28,0:19:54.88,Original,,0,0,0,,where it's heated for 50 seconds at 55 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.00,0:19:57.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后拍刃由手工修整
Dialogue: 1,0:19:56.00,0:19:57.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The blade is then worked by hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.88,0:20:02.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,新拍刃与著名冰球选手球棍的样板比对
Dialogue: 1,0:19:58.88,0:20:02.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The new blade is compared with the pattern of the famous hockey player's stick
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.16,0:20:05.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,以获得完全一致的弧度
Dialogue: 1,0:20:03.16,0:20:05.24,Original,,0,0,0,,to obtain precisely the same curvature.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.12,0:20:18.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在拍刃被砂磨到所需厚度
Dialogue: 1,0:20:16.12,0:20:18.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the blade is sanded down to the desired thickness,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.68,0:20:28.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,但拍刃还需加固
Dialogue: 1,0:20:26.68,0:20:28.60,Original,,0,0,0,,but the blade must also be reinforced.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.80,0:20:32.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,用环氧树脂浸泡一块玻璃纤维布
Dialogue: 1,0:20:29.80,0:20:32.60,Original,,0,0,0,,A fiberglass cloth is soaked with epoxy resin.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.28,0:20:42.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,排掉气泡后，放入烘箱在 32 摄氏度下干燥 24 小时
Dialogue: 1,0:20:36.28,0:20:42.20,Original,,0,0,0,,They get rid of air bubbles, then put it into an oven to dry at 32 degrees over 24 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.64,0:20:55.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,多余的玻璃纤维硬化后用带锯裁掉
Dialogue: 1,0:20:51.64,0:20:55.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The surplus fiberglass hardens and is cut with a bandsaw.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.96,0:20:58.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这项工作需要手稳
Dialogue: 1,0:20:55.96,0:20:58.00,Original,,0,0,0,,A steady hand is needed to do this job.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.40,0:21:05.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,用这台圆盘砂光机进行精修
Dialogue: 1,0:21:03.40,0:21:05.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Finishing is done with this circular sander.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.40,0:21:15.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，拍刃浸入环氧树脂，获得漂亮的光泽
Dialogue: 1,0:21:11.40,0:21:15.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, the blade is dipped into this epoxy resin to give it a nice luster.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.36,0:21:18.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,剩下的就是上漆
Dialogue: 1,0:21:16.36,0:21:18.36,Original,,0,0,0,,All that remains is a paint job.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.68,0:21:23.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,公司标志通过丝网印刷印上
Dialogue: 1,0:21:20.68,0:21:23.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Company logos are applied via silk screening.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.72,0:21:29.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,除了 6000 款职业冰球选手的个人球型
Dialogue: 1,0:21:25.72,0:21:29.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Besides the 6,000 personal models of professional hockey players,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.28,0:21:33.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家公司还生产 65 款其他型号
Dialogue: 1,0:21:30.28,0:21:33.44,Original,,0,0,0,,this company produces 65 other models.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.44,0:21:39.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,每周生产约 4万根球棍，也就是每年 160 万根
Dialogue: 1,0:21:33.44,0:21:39.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Each week, they make about 40,000 sticks, which means 1,600,000 a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.52,0:21:44.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这可真是大量的劲射
Dialogue: 1,0:21:40.52,0:21:44.80,Original,,0,0,0,,That's a lot of slap shots.
